Template: multiflexi-eventor/nodered_webhook_url
Type: string
Description: Node-RED HTTP-in webhook URL:
 The Event Processor can forward webhook change events and finished jobs to a
 Node-RED HTTP-in endpoint.
 .
 Enter the full URL of the Node-RED HTTP-in node (for example
 https://nodered.example.com/multiflexi). Leave empty to disable the bridge.

Template: multiflexi-eventor/nodered_token
Type: password
Description: Node-RED shared secret token:
 Optional secret sent as the X-MultiFlexi-Token header with every request to
 the Node-RED endpoint. Leave empty to send no token.

Template: multiflexi-eventor/nodered_forward_changes
Type: boolean
Default: true
Description: Forward incoming webhook changes to Node-RED?
 If true, incoming webhook change events are forwarded to Node-RED in addition
 to finished jobs. If false, only finished jobs are forwarded.
